{"time": "2026-09-03T15:51:44.113122", "type": "action", "data": "{\"tool\": {\"name\": \"bash\", \"input\": {\"command\": \"\\n# Create a normalized version of the C++ file\\n# This will:\\n# 1. Remove C++ style comments (//)\\n# 2. Remove C style comments (/* */)\\n# 3. Remove leading/trailing whitespace\\n# 4. Remove empty lines\\n# 5. Normalize whitespace (multiple spaces to single space)\\n\\n# Using gcc preprocessor to remove comments and then normalize whitespace\\ngcc -fpreprocessed -dD -E -P /tmp/submission.cpp 2>/dev/null | \\\\\\n  sed 's/^[[:space:]]*//g' | \\\\  # Remove leading whitespace\\n  sed 's/[[:space:]]*$//g' | \\\\  # Remove trailing whitespace\\n  sed '/^$/d' | \\\\                # Remove empty lines\\n  sed 's/[[:space:]]\\\\+/ /g' > /tmp/normalized.cpp  # Normalize multiple spaces to single space\\n\\necho \\\"=== Normalized code ===\\\"\\ncat /tmp/normalized.cpp\\necho \\\"\\\"\\necho \\\"=== MD5 sum of normalized code ===\\\"\\nmd5sum /tmp/normalized.cpp | cut -d' ' -f1\\n\"}}}"}
